{"id": "De6TIvERduV", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Ram cut off Ravana's head… it GREW BACK! 😱🏹 How did Ram finally defeat Ravana? | Ramayan Part 12 of 12, the FINALE\n\n🐎 Ravana fought from a chariot, Ram on foot. So Indra sent his own chariot, driven by Matali. (Valmiki Ramayana, Yuddha Kanda 102)\n☀️ The sage Agastya taught Ram a hymn to the Sun, the Aditya Hridayam. Ram chanted it 3 times and felt new strength. (Yuddha 105)\n🔁 Ram cut off Ravana's heads… but they kept growing back. Again and again, a hundred times! (Yuddha 107)\n✨ Then Matali said: \"Use the Brahmastra!\" Ram charged it with mantras and let it fly, blazing like the Sun. It struck Ravana's heart, and Ravana fell from his chariot. The arrow flew back into Ram's quiver. (Yuddha 108)\n🌸 The gods showered flowers! (Yuddha 108)\n👑 Ram, Sita and Lakshman flew home to Ayodhya on the Pushpaka, and Ram became king. (Yuddha 121–128)\n\n🙏 That's the whole Ramayan in 12 parts! Missed one? Start from Part 1 on our page, and Follow @therishikatha for the next series.\n\n📚 Rishi Katha picture books tell our gods' stories for kids, in simple words and bright pictures → rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\n💬 Comment JAI SHRI RAM 🙏 and tell us: which story should our next series be?\n🔖 Save this, and share the series with a kid you love 🧡\n\n#ramayan #ramayana #shriram #ravana #adityahridayam #brahmastra #valmikiramayana #yuddhakanda #jaishriram #hanuman #sita #sanatandharma #hindumythology #ramayanseries #rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792917668, "like_count": 2971, "comment_count": 54, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-3429006210616667a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 50.331, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-2.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQOrAlrCJqWVXB5GrW_7nAkQ0